00:03:22,825 --> 00:03:25,823
browser, you can click Connect to confirm

85
00:03:25,871 --> 00:03:28,100
that you want to add this VPS to your

86
00:03:28,212 --> 00:03:31,260
tailnet, to your Tailscale network in the

87
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:31,516
end.

88
00:03:32,366 --> 00:03:33,954
So here I got the success message

89
00:03:34,692 --> 00:03:34,884
and now

90
00:03:35,429 --> 00:03:37,899
this VPS is part of my Tailscale network.

91
00:03:38,492 --> 00:03:40,657
Now what exactly does this mean?

92
00:03:41,523 --> 00:03:44,009
This means that now I can find it in my

93
00:03:44,314 --> 00:03:47,297
devices list here in the Tailscale app on my

94
00:03:47,297 --> 00:03:49,029
Mac here and the same of course on Windows.

95
00:03:49,686 --> 00:03:52,074
Just as I find my MacBook Pro here.

96
00:03:53,147 --> 00:03:55,471
And each device here has an IP,

97
00:03:56,256 --> 00:03:59,077
a private IP which can't be reached from the

98
00:03:59,077 --> 00:04:00,022
public internet.

99
00:04:01,464 --> 00:04:04,060
And my MacBook, for example, also has an IP.

100
00:04:04,669 --> 00:04:04,717
I

101
00:04:05,246 --> 00:04:07,938
blurred it here. It shouldn't be required,

102
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:09,989
but I wanna be extra safe, but there is an

103
00:04:10,037 --> 00:04:13,050
IP here too. So now with Tailscale running

104
00:04:13,098 --> 00:04:15,663
on the VPS and running on my Mac, and the

105
00:04:15,663 --> 00:04:18,491
VPS added to my Tailscale network, I can go

106
00:04:18,491 --> 00:04:20,966
to the firewalls here on my server if you're

107
00:04:20,966 --> 00:04:22,910
using a provider that has a feature like

108
00:04:23,119 --> 00:04:24,051
Hetzner has here,

109
00:04:24,822 --> 00:04:25,658
and I can edit that.

110
00:04:26,734 --> 00:04:30,302
And what I wanna do here is actually delete

111
00:04:30,446 --> 00:04:32,005
this entire rule here

112
00:04:32,535 --> 00:04:33,724
and instead add a new rule.

113
00:04:34,367 --> 00:04:35,235
And for that rule,

114
00:04:35,894 --> 00:04:38,175
we wanna switch the protocol to UDP

115
00:04:38,882 --> 00:04:40,698
and set the port to 4101.

116
00:04:43,459 --> 00:04:45,947
This may look weird because it's a different

117
00:04:45,947 --> 00:04:48,017
