118
00:04:48,017 --> 00:04:50,649
is that in the future, our connection will

119
00:04:50,697 --> 00:04:53,121
no longer go directly from our machine

120
00:04:53,393 --> 00:04:55,544
through the public internet to this server,

121
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,561
but instead it will go through the Tailscale

122
00:04:58,706 --> 00:04:59,251
network.

123
00:04:59,829 --> 00:05:01,675
And that network will internally

124
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,194
kind of forward the request, you could say,

125
00:05:04,403 --> 00:05:06,987
via this protocol and port to the

126
00:05:07,517 --> 00:05:10,150
target machine. So that's why we need to set

127
00:05:10,664 --> 00:05:11,660
this rule here

128
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:12,543
in our

129
00:05:13,218 --> 00:05:15,129
firewall, our Hetzner firewall.

130
00:05:16,429 --> 00:05:19,432
If you are using UFW instead because you're

131
00:05:19,432 --> 00:05:21,665
not using a provider that comes with its own

132
00:05:21,729 --> 00:05:22,194
firewall,

133
00:05:22,933 --> 00:05:26,514
what you would have to do is run sudo ufw

134
00:05:26,948 --> 00:05:28,602
allow-in on

135
00:05:29,276 --> 00:05:30,561
tailscale0.

136
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:33,789
This is a virtual network device in the end

137
00:05:33,789 --> 00:05:36,069
that's added by Tailscale since we ran

138
00:05:36,198 --> 00:05:38,734
tailscale up on the VPS, this was added

139
00:05:39,407 --> 00:05:41,252
and that will automatically add all the

140
00:05:41,317 --> 00:05:43,354
required rules, which you can double check

141
00:05:43,418 --> 00:05:46,563
by then running sudo ufw status verbose

142
00:05:47,975 --> 00:05:50,590
and you see these 2 Tailscale rules here.

143
00:05:51,504 --> 00:05:52,290
That is what you need.

144
00:05:52,964 --> 00:05:55,515
You could then remove these SSH rules, but

145
00:05:55,515 --> 00:05:57,472
let's not do that just yet to

146
00:05:58,403 --> 00:06:00,505
leave ourselves a door open in case

147
00:06:00,505 --> 00:06:02,478
something is wrong and we locked ourselves

148
00:06:02,671 --> 00:06:02,895
out.

149
00:06:03,714 --> 00:06:05,993
What you'll also need to do is edit your

150
00:06:06,266 --> 00:06:08,899
entry in the SSH config file if you're using

151
00:06:08,995 --> 00:06:09,252
that,

152
00:06:09,814 --> 00:06:11,403
because we're still trying to connect to

153
00:06:11,403 --> 00:06:13,843
this IP and that will no longer work when

154
00:06:13,907 --> 00:06:16,058
we're going through the Tailscale network.

155
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:17,166
Instead,

156
00:06:17,904 --> 00:06:20,794
the idea is that each device that's part of

157
00:06:20,794 --> 00:06:23,764
our Tailscale network gets its own private

158
00:06:23,844 --> 00:06:24,181
IP.

159
00:06:24,743 --> 00:06:28,339
Indeed, you can see that on your Mac or your

160
00:06:28,339 --> 00:06:30,634
Windows machine if you start the Tailscale

161
00:06:30,827 --> 00:06:31,003
app,

162
00:06:31,565 --> 00:06:33,219
you can see a list of devices here.

163
00:06:33,797 --> 00:06:35,420
For example, here's my MacBook Pro

164
00:06:36,143 --> 00:06:39,389
and here's that VPS I added. So now it's

165
00:06:39,437 --> 00:06:40,353
that VPS

166
00:06:40,964 --> 00:06:42,908
private IP here, which you can copy by

167
00:06:42,908 --> 00:06:43,454
clicking here.

168
00:06:44,483 --> 00:06:46,460
That is what goes into the config file now

169
00:06:47,697 --> 00:06:49,609
because that's the IP we're now connecting

170
00:06:49,625 --> 00:06:49,866
to

171
00:06:50,445 --> 00:06:53,079
via Tailscale in the end. So you wanna save

172
00:06:53,111 --> 00:06:53,974
that config file.

173
00:06:55,477 --> 00:06:58,475
And now in a new window, if I try to connect

174
00:06:58,475 --> 00:07:00,941
via SSH, I again have to confirm the

175
00:07:00,957 --> 00:07:02,521
identity of this host because this is an

176
00:07:02,521 --> 00:07:03,359
unknown IP. I haven't used it before.

177
00:07:05,693 --> 00:07:08,858
But if I hit yes, if you did start Tailscale

178
00:07:09,131 --> 00:07:11,750
on the VPS and you did set up your firewall

179
00:07:11,862 --> 00:07:13,967
as I showed you and Tailscale is running on

180
00:07:13,967 --> 00:07:16,634
your Mac too and you edited this config file

181
00:07:16,698 --> 00:07:17,292
as I showed you,

182
00:07:17,887 --> 00:07:19,863
this connection should still work but now

183
00:07:20,778 --> 00:07:22,385
